## 8. Content workflow

Text lives in files, never in components.

- `messages/*.json`: website text, grouped by page/section (`home.title`, `contact.hours`, `meta.homeTitle`). Current groups: `nav` (header links, mobile menu labels), `localeSwitcher`, `menu`, `about`, `contact`.
- `data/menu.ts`: dishes and categories
- `data/site.ts`: brand name, address, phone, hours, socials (same in every language; only the labels go in JSON)

Process:
1. The client's owner writes everything in **Montenegrin first** (`messages/me.json` and the `me` fields in `menu.ts`).
2. Until translations exist, copy `me.json` into `en/it/ru/tr.json` so the site builds.
3. When the Montenegrin content is final, translate into EN, IT, RU, TR. Keep keys identical and do not touch `{placeholders}` or HTML tags.
4. Run `npm run i18n:check`.
5. Native speakers proofread IT, RU, TR (food terms and allergen information especially).

**`data/menu.ts` format** (the example is placeholder only):
```ts
type L = Record<'me' | 'en' | 'it' | 'ru' | 'tr', string>;

export const menu: {
  id: string;
  title: L;
  items: { name: L; desc?: L; price: number }[];
}[] = [
  {
    id: 'crepes',
    title: { me: 'Palačinke', en: 'Crepes', it: 'Crêpes', ru: 'Блины', tr: 'Krep' },
    items: [
      {
        name: { me: 'Palačinka s nutelom', en: 'Crepe with Nutella', it: 'Crêpe alla Nutella', ru: 'Блин с нутеллой', tr: 'Nutellalı krep' },
        price: 0, // TODO real price
      },
    ],
  },
];
```
Prices are numbers in EUR, shown with `toFixed(2)` and the € sign.

