## 9. Design system

**Look:** warm, friendly, sweet. Round shapes echo the circular logo. Cream background on every page, maroon as the main color, peach for highlights. Restraint: one memorable element per screen, everything else quiet. The header (a maroon bar with the logo badge) is the site's one strong element; page sections stay on cream.

### Colors (sampled from the logo)

| Role | Hex | Use |
|---|---|---|
| Maroon | `#892E30` | Primary: buttons, prices, active states, links; header bar and mobile menu panel. The logo's exact maroon |
| Peach | `#FFD29F` | Secondary: chips, highlights, section backgrounds; header line and active header link |
| Cream | `#FFF9F2` | Page background (all pages); header link text |
| Cocoa | `#2E1517` | Body text |

Contrast: cocoa on cream 16.3:1, maroon on cream 8.0:1, cream on maroon 8.0:1 (header links), maroon on peach 6.0:1, peach on maroon 6.0:1 (active header link), `muted-foreground` on cream 5.9:1. **Never put peach text on a light background** (peach on cream is 1.3:1).

Tokens are defined in `app/globals.css` (shadcn variables overridden with the brand values, plus `bg-brand-maroon`, `bg-brand-peach`, `bg-brand-cream`, `bg-brand-cocoa` and the matching `text-`/`border-` classes). Use semantic classes (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`) first and brand classes only when needed. No white anywhere: cards and popovers (`--card`, `--popover`) are cream `#FFF9F2` too. They stand out from the page only through their shadow/ring or border, so keep those when restyling.

### Typography

- Headings: **Nunito**, weights 700 to 900, rounded terminals like the logo (`font-heading`, applied to h1 to h4 globally)
- Body: **Inter** (`font-sans`)
- Both must cover `latin`, `latin-ext`, `cyrillic` (č ć š ž đ, ğ ı ş, Russian)
- Line length under about 70 characters. Sentence case. No ALL CAPS eyebrow labels above headings.

**Fonts are self-hosted with `next/font/local`. Do not go back to `next/font/google`.** With Turbopack, Google Fonts sometimes returns `fonts.gstatic.com/l/font?kit=...&skey=...` URLs, which break the build with `Module not found: Can't resolve '@vercel/turbopack-next/internal/font/google/font'` / `next/font/google queries have exactly one entry`. The broken CSS is also saved in `.next/dev`, so the error survives restarts.

**`lib/fonts.ts`**
```ts
import localFont from "next/font/local"

export const nunito = localFont({
  src: "../app/fonts/Nunito.woff2",
  weight: "700 900",
  variable: "--font-nunito",
  display: "swap",
})

export const inter = localFont({
  src: "../app/fonts/Inter.woff2",
  weight: "100 900",
  variable: "--font-inter",
  display: "swap",
})
```
The files in `app/fonts/` are variable woff2 fonts built from the originals in github.com/google/fonts (`ofl/nunito`, `ofl/inter`), cut down to the latin + latin-ext + cyrillic character ranges. Nunito is limited to weights 700–900 (50 KB). Inter has all weights 100–900, with its optical-size axis fixed at 14 (142 KB). Their OFL licence files sit next to them. To add a weight or a font, build a new file the same way (the npm package `subset-font` works; this machine has no Python pip/venv).

In `app/[locale]/layout.tsx`: `<html lang={...} className={cn(nunito.variable, inter.variable, ...)}>`. The variable names must stay `--font-nunito` and `--font-inter`, because `globals.css` maps them to `--font-heading` and `--font-sans`. Do not rename them to `--font-sans`.

### Shape and layout

- Radius: large. Cards `rounded-2xl`/`rounded-3xl`, buttons and chips pill-shaped (`rounded-full`).
- Spacing: 8px grid, sections `py-16 md:py-24`, content `max-w-6xl`, menu page `max-w-2xl`.
- Mobile-first. Design at 375px width first, then scale up.
- Russian and Italian text is 20 to 30% longer than Montenegrin: no fixed-width buttons or headings.

### Components

Install with the CLI as needed: `button`, `tabs`, `card`, `badge`, `sheet` (mobile nav), `dropdown-menu`, `separator`, `skeleton`. Installed so far: `button`, `sheet`, `dropdown-menu`.

The generated components contain some hardcoded English (for example the Sheet close button's `sr-only` "Close"). Do not ship that text: turn the built-in part off (`showCloseButton={false}`) and render your own with a translated label.

### Logo and images

- Header: the real logo (`public/logoharis.png`, static import) via `next/image`, with `site.name` as `alt`. Do not type the brand name as text instead of the logo.
- Favicon: square version of the logo as `app/icon.png`.
- OG image: `public/og.jpg`, 1200x630, logo on cream.
- Food photos: warm natural light, close-ups, one consistent aspect ratio, `rounded-2xl`, always `next/image`, compressed.

### Header (`components/layout/site-header.tsx`)

Based on the printed menu: a dark bar with the round logo badge hanging over a peach line. Built and checked at 375px, 640px and 1280px.

- Bar: `bg-brand-maroon`, `h-16` (`md:h-20`), 2px `border-brand-peach` at the bottom. Content `max-w-6xl`, `px-4`.
- Logo badge: `h-24` (`md:h-34`), absolutely positioned at the left and centred on the peach line, so its lower half hangs into the page. The first section of every page needs top padding of at least 48px (68px from `md`), which `py-16 md:py-24` already gives. Do not go above about `h-32`/`md:h-40`, or the badge pokes out of the top of the bar.
- Links: Meni · O nama · Kontakt (`nav.*` messages), Nunito bold, cream text. The current page is peach with `aria-current="page"` (`nav-links.tsx`, a client component because it reads the pathname).
- Right side: links (from `sm`), then the language switcher. Below `sm`: globe + hamburger, and the links open in a `Sheet` from the right (maroon panel, own translated close button, closes when a link is clicked).
- **Not sticky.** A sticky header would put the hanging badge over the menu page's sticky category chips.
- Focus on the bar: the default focus ring is maroon and invisible on the maroon bar, so header controls use a peach outline/ring (`header-styles.ts` for the icon buttons).
- The server component `site-header.tsx` renders three client parts: `nav-links.tsx`, `mobile-nav.tsx` and `language-switcher.tsx`.

### Language switcher

A **dropdown** (shadcn `DropdownMenu`). The button shows the current language's flag and code (`ME`, `EN`, ...). The list shows a flag and code for EN, RU, IT, TR, ME (`switcherLocales`), with a check close to the current one: the list is `w-auto min-w-(--anchor-width)`, so it fits its content instead of the default `min-w-48`. Both use Nunito bold. Inline pills do not fit on a phone next to the logo.
- Flags: round SVGs from circle-flags (MIT, licence in `public/flags/LICENSE.md`), static imports in `language-switcher.tsx`, decorative (`alt=""`) because the code and name carry the meaning. **EN uses the UK flag.** Do not use emoji flags: Windows shows them as plain letters. Implementation (`components/layout/language-switcher.tsx`): `useLocale` from next-intl, `usePathname`/`useRouter` from `@/i18n/navigation`, a `DropdownMenuRadioGroup`, and `router.replace(pathname, { locale })` inside `startTransition`. Notes:
- Base UI radio items do not close the menu by default: each item has `closeOnClick`.
- Screen readers: the button contains a `sr-only` `localeSwitcher.label` before the visible code, so its name is "Izaberite jezik ME". Each item has the code plus a `sr-only` native name ("EN English") and `lang={hreflang[l]}`, so the name is pronounced correctly. Keep the visible code inside the accessible name: do not replace it with an `aria-label`.
- Verified: choosing English on `/meni` goes to `/en/menu`.

### Menu page (`app/[locale]/meni/page.tsx`)

- Sticky horizontal category chips (pill-shaped, active one maroon, inactive peach), scrolling horizontally on small screens. Anchor links to each category section. The header is not sticky, so the chips stick at `top-0`. When they exist, set `scroll-padding-top` in `globals.css` to the chips' height (it is still `7rem`, sized for a sticky header + chips).
- Narrow single column (`max-w-2xl`).
- Item row: name, optional short description in `text-muted-foreground`, price in bold maroon on the right.
- Optional photo per item. Small `Badge`s for vegan, new, allergens.
- Allergen note at the bottom, translated.
- Must load fast on mobile data.

### Motion and accessibility

**One motion style for the whole site**, defined at the top of `app/globals.css`. Use it everywhere and do not invent new timings:
- **Timing:** 200ms with `ease-brand` (`cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1)`, fast start, soft landing). It is set as Tailwind's default, so every `transition-colors`, `transition-opacity`, `transition` etc. gets it automatically. **Never add `duration-*` or `ease-*` classes.**
- **Popups that open and close** (dropdowns, popovers, selects, dialogs): add `transition-popup`, a fade plus a slight zoom (96% to 100%) from the trigger. It relies on Base UI's `data-starting-style`/`data-ending-style`. The dropdown menu uses it.
- **Sheets/drawers:** fade plus a short slide, with the same default timing (`components/ui/sheet.tsx`).
- **Content that appears** (loaded or swapped in): `animate-fade-in` (opacity only).
- **Hover/active states:** `transition-colors` (as on the header links).
- The generated shadcn components were changed to use this: the `tw-animate-css` classes (`animate-in`, `fade-in-0`, `zoom-in-95`, `duration-100`...) were removed from `dropdown-menu.tsx`, and the fixed durations/easing from `sheet.tsx`. Do the same to every new shadcn component you add.
- **Reduced motion:** `transition-popup` and the sheet fade only (no zoom/slide) when `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` is set. Keep that for anything new (`motion-reduce:transition-opacity`).
- Verified in Chrome: the dropdown fades in and out in about 200ms; the sheet and its overlay use 200ms + `ease-brand`; with reduced motion only opacity transitions.

Still little motion overall: no fade-and-slide on every section, no hover animation on every card. One deliberate moment at most.
- Visible keyboard focus (already set in `globals.css`), alt text on all images, `aria-label`s translated.

